@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {

  usecase "View Available\nStudy Rooms" as UC1
  usecase "Book Study Room" as UC2
  usecase "Cancel Own Booking" as UC3
  usecase "Review Study Room\nUsage" as UC4
  usecase "Block / Unblock\nStudy Room" as UC5
  usecase "Check Booking\nTime Availability" as UC6
  usecase "Confirm Successful\nBooking" as UC7
}

Student --> UC1
Student --> UC2
Student --> UC3

Administrator --> UC4
Administrator --> UC5

' why: US-02 and US-06 require booking availability and overlap validation
UC2 ..> UC6 : <<include>>

' why: R4 requires every successful booking to produce a confirmation
UC2 ..> UC7 : <<include>>

note right of UC2
R1: Start is in the future;
duration > 0 and <= 2 hours.
R2: Same-room active bookings
cannot overlap.
R3: Blocked rooms cannot
accept new bookings.
end note

note right of UC5
R3: Blocking a room prevents
new bookings; unblocking
makes it available again.
end note

note bottom
Assumptions:
1. Touching bookings do not overlap:
   one booking may start exactly when another ends.
2. Blocking a room prevents new bookings
   but does not cancel existing bookings.
3. Students may cancel only their own bookings.
4. No out-of-scope features are modeled.
end note

@enduml